eal-time category statistics of the specified test case instance.\', \'guidance\': \'Call /v1/cl/stats/category/search to get a list of statistical categories that can be used to analyze the results of this test. This API requires a valid session_id and timestamp (valid within 10 minutes). The request body should contain the specific search criteria as defined in the StatsCategorySearchRequest schema.\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'BASE_URL\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'API base without trailing slash\'}, {\'name\': \'TIMESTAMP\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'unix timestamp, expired in 10 minutes\'}, {\'name\': \'SESSION_ID\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'allocated session id\'}, {\'name\': \'body\', \'type\': \'object\', \'description\': \'request body following the StatsCategorySearchRequest schema\', \'schema\': {\'$ref\': \'#/definitions/statsapi.StatsCategorySearchRequest\'}}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'response_body\', \'type\': \'object\', \'description\': \'The response body follows the StatsCategorySearchResponse schema\', \'schema\': {\'$ref\': \'#/definitions/statsapi.StatsCategorySearchResponse\'}}]}, {\'step\': 1, \'description\': \'Search for the statistics history of a specific testcase instance\', \'guidance\': \'Call /v1/cl/stats/search with POST method to retrieve statistical data. This API requires a valid session_id and a timestamp (valid within 10 minutes) as query parameters, and a request body conforming to StatsSearchRequest schema.\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'BASE_URL\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'API base without trailing slash\'}, {\'name\': \'TIMESTAMP\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'unix timestamp, expired in 10 minutes\'}, {\'name\': \'SESSION_ID\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'allocated session id\'}, {\'name\': \'body\', \'type\': \'object\', \'description\': \'request body conforming to StatsSearchRequest schema\', \'schema\': {\'$ref\': \'#/definitions/statsapi.StatsSearchRequest\'}}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'response\', \'type\': \'object\', \'description\': \'response body conforming to StatsSearchResponse schema\', \'schema\': {\'$ref\': \'#/definitions/statsapi.StatsSearchResponse\'}}]}, {\'step\': 9, \'description\': \'User logout from the system\', \'guidance\': \'Call /v1/cl/user/logout to safely log out after completing all test steps. This API requires a valid session_id and timestamp (valid for 10 minutes) as query parameters, and a body request that conforms to alps.UserLogoutRequest schema.\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'BASE_URL\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'API base without trailing slash\'}, {\'name\': \'TIMESTAMP\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'unix timestamp, expired in 10 minutes, type is int\'}, {\'name\': \'SESSION_ID\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'allocated session id\'}, {\'name\': \'body\', \'type\': \'object\', \'description\': \'Request body conforming to alps.UserLogoutRequest schema\', \'schema\': {\'$ref\': \'#/definitions/alps.UserLogoutRequest\'}}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'response\', \'type\': \'object\', \'description\': \'Response body conforming to alps.UserLogoutResponse schema\', \'schema\': {\'$ref\': \'#/definitions/alps.UserLogoutResponse\'}}]}]\n</RAW_TESTCASE>\n\n\n#### 2. 目标测试用例标准格式\n<STANDARD_FORMAT>\n{\'name\': \'Simple testcase\', \'demand\': \'testcase v0.0.0\', \'tester\': \'XRT Darpeng\', \'steps\': [{\'step\': 0, \'description\': \'Set some parameters.\', \'guidance\': \'Set some basic parameters, such as Base_url, username and password\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'BASE_URL\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'The BASE_URL is https://10.99.80.111:7070\'}, {\'name\': \'USERNAME\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'The USERNAME is admin\'}, {\'name\': \'PASSWORD\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'The PASSWORD is admin\'}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'session_id\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'session_id from response\'}]}, {\'step\': 1, \'description\': \'Login WITH signature\', \'guidance\': \'Call /v1/cl/user/login with signature, which should be calculated with password and something else\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'BASE_URL\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'API base without trailing slash\'}, {\'name\': \'USERNAME\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'username for login\'}, {\'name\': \'PASSWORD\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'password for login\'}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'session_id\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'session_id from response\'}]}, {\'step\': 2, \'description\': \'List all network neighbors\', \'guidance\': \'Call /v1/cl/network/list to search all network neighbors and extract the default network neighbor. Output its network_id.\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'session_id\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'session_id from response\'}, {\'name\': \'timestamp\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'unix timestamp, expired in 10 minutes\'}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'network_id\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'Default network neighbor ID extracted from response\'}]}, {\'step\': 3, \'description\': \'Fetch network details\', \'guidance\': \'Call /v1/cl/network/fetch with network_id to retrieve full configuration, including ipv4_static_host_list.\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'session_id\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'session_id from response\'}, {\'name\': \'timestamp\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'unix timestamp, expired in 10 minutes\'}, {\'name\': \'network_id\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'ID of the network to fetch\'}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'ipv4_static_host_list\', \'type\': \'list[dict]\', \'description\': \'Static IPv4 hosts returned by the API\'}]}, {\'step\': 4, \'description\': \'Fetch network component tags\', \'guidance\': \'Call /v1/cl/network/tags/fetch with network_id to retrieve component tags.\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'session_id\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'session_id from response\'}, {\'name\': \'timestamp\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'unix timestamp, expired in 10 minutes\'}, {\'name\': \'network_id\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'Network ID whose component tags will be fetched\'}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'component_tags\', \'type\': \'list[str]\', \'description\': \'List of component tags associated with the given network\'}]}, {\'step\': 5, \'description\': \'Create DDoS attack component\', \'guidance\': \'Call /v1/cl/testcase/component/create with type=2 to create a DDoS component. Extract returned configuration parameters.\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'session_id\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'session_id from response\'}, {\'name\': \'timestamp\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'unix timestamp, expired in 10 minutes\'}, {\'name\': \'type\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'Component type; 2 represents DDoS attack component\'}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'ddos_attack_component_config\', \'type\': \'object\', \'description\': "The detailed configuration information for the ddos_attack component includes the following sections:\'basic\',\'load_profile\',\'attack_profile\',\'data_rate\',\'super_flow\',\'src_port\',\'delay_start\',\'clean_duration\'"}]}, {\'step\': 6, \'description\': \'List all DDoS attack profiles\', \'guidance\': \'Call /v1/cl/ddos/attack/profile/list to retrieve all attack profiles, then Select an attack profile from the returned results that matches or contains the attack_name. Output profile_id and profile_name.\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'session_id\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'session_id from response\'}, {\'name\': \'timestamp\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'unix timestamp, expired in 10 minutes\'}, {\'name\': \'attack_name\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'keyword to identify the required attack profile\'}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'profile_id\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'ID of the attack profile matching the test requirement\'}, {\'name\': \'profile_name\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'Name of the matched attack profile\'}]}, {\'step\': 7, \'description\': \'Fetch a testcase configuration\', \'guidance\': \'Call /v1/cl/testcase/fetch with testcase_id to retrieve complete configuration parameters.\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'session_id\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'session_id from response\'}, {\'name\': \'timestamp\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'unix timestamp, expired in 10 minutes\'}, {\'name\': \'testcase_id\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'ID of the testcase to fetch\'}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'testcase_config\', \'type\': \'object\', \'description\': \'Configuration of the specified testcase\'}]}, {\'step\': 8, \'description\': \'Save testcase after modifying DDoS attack profile\', \'guidance\': \'The parameters for the /v1/cl/testcase/save endpoint are formed by merging the testcase_config and ddos_attack_component_config objects, update the profile_id in ddos_attack_compoent_config. Output the new testcase_id.\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'session_id\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'session_id from response\'}, {\'name\': \'timestamp\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'unix timestamp, expired in 10 minutes\'}, {\'name\': \'testcase_config\', \'type\': \'object\', \'description\': \'Configuration of the specified testcase\'}, {\'name\': \'ddos_attack_component_config\', \'type\': \'object\', \'description\': "The detailed configuration information for the ddos_attack component includes the following sections: \'basic\',\'load_profile\',\'attack_profile\',\'data_rate\',\'super_flow\',\'src_port\',\'delay_start\',\'clean_duration\'"}, {\'name\': \'profile_id\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'DDoS attack profile ID used to update the testcase\'}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'testcase_id\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'ID of the saved or updated testcase\'}]}, {\'step\': 9, \'description\': \'Run the testcase\', \'guidance\': \'Call /v1/cl/testcase/run with testcase_id and testcase_name to start executing the testcase.\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'session_id\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'session_id from response\'}, {\'name\': \'timestamp\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'unix timestamp, expired in 10 minutes\'}, {\'name\': \'testcase_id\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'ID of the testcase to run\'}, {\'name\': \'testcase_name\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'name of the testcase\'}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'instance_id\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'testcase instance id\'}]}, {\'step\': 10, \'description\': \'Logout current user\', \'guidance\': \'Call /v1/cl/user/logout with the current username (e.g., admin) to terminate the session.\', \'input\': [{\'name\': \'session_id\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'session_id from response\'}, {\'name\': \'timestamp\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'unix timestamp, expired in 10 minutes\'}, {\'name\': \'USERNAME\', \'type\': \'str\', \'description\': \'Username to logout, such as admin\'}], \'output\': [{\'name\': \'code\', \'type\': \'int\', \'description\': \'Returned logout result status, response code, zero for success, non-zero for errors\'}]}]}\n</STANDARD_FORMAT>\n---\n\n### 二、修改原则（必须严格遵守）\n\n1. **只做结构与表达层面的修改**\n   - 允许：顺序调整、格式补全\n   - 不允许：引入新的测试步骤、新的测试数据\n\n2. **测试语义保持完全一致**\n   - 每个步骤的输入、操作、预期含义不得改变\n\n3. **对齐标准格式**\n   - 层级结构与标准格式一致\n\n---\n\n### 三、输出要求\n\n1. 仅输出【修改后的测试用例】\n2. 输出格式必须【完全符合标准格式】\n3. 不要输出任何解释、分析、对比说明或多余文本\n4. 保持字段顺序与标准格式一致\n5. 输出必须是合法的 JSON，可被程序直接解析\n\n---\n\n### 四、输出示例风格（仅作参考）\n- 使用清晰、正式、测试文档风格的描述\n- 避免口语化或推理性语言\n\n---\n\n现在请开始修改测试用例。'}]}}
